message: "If you use this software or these results, please cite it as below."
title: "Tumor proliferation masks the prognostic association of CYB5R3 in hepatocellular carcinoma: pre-registered analysis code and results"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nam"
    given-names: "Soon Woo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5562-4775"
    affiliation: "Hepatobiliary Unit, Division of Gastroenterology, Department of Internal Medicine, Incheon St. Mary's Hospital, College of Medicine, The Catholic University of Korea, Seoul, Republic of Korea"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - hepatocellular carcinoma
  - CYB5R3
  - prognosis
  - cell proliferation
  - confounding
  - molecular subclass
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered R analysis of CYB5R3 in hepatocellular carcinoma using TCGA-LIHC
  and GSE14520. The pre-registered hypothesis, that Hoshida molecular subclass
  explains the discordance between histologic grade and survival, is rejected on
  all four counts. Labelled post hoc analyses then show that grade is not
  prognostic in TCGA-LIHC and that the grade trend tracks proliferation, and that
  proliferation negatively confounds the association between CYB5R3 and survival.
  That finding is tested in GSE14520 under a rule fixed in advance. This repository
  contains the decision rules, the analysis scripts, the frozen subclass templates,
  every result file, the run logs and the manuscript figures.
